<title>CHINA: Tai Fook announces first final results.</title>
<headline>Tai Fook announces first final results.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   31.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.5</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil</p>
<p>    Net			    87.77</p>
<p>    Turnover		     309.40</p>
<p>    Company name		 Tai Fook Group Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 12-19</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   September 26</p>
<p>NOTE - Financial services concern Tai Fook was listed on the Stock Exchange on August 6, 1996.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one 1999 warrant for every five shares held. The warrants carry rights to subscribe for new shares at an initial subscription price of HK$4.125 per share at any time after dealing in the warrants commence -- expected to be September 29, 1997 -- to August 31, 1999.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 8.5 H.K. cents (including an interim dividend of two cents).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
